IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Australian time rules for nine jurisdictions, in one self-contained module.
--
-- THIS FILE IS THE ORIGINAL.
-- It lives at subjects/au/_jurisdiction/library/au-time-rules.l4 in legalese/commons.
-- A later encoding holds a byte-identical copy of this file beside its own modules,
-- because an IMPORT names a module and only the importing file's own folder is searched.
-- That encoding records, in its NOTES, the path of this original and its sha256.
--
-- This module is assembled from nine source modules, the time module of each jurisdiction's
-- interpretation Act, as they stand in legalese/commons at main ece722340.
-- The nine are listed, with their paths, sha256 values and line counts, in au-time-rules.MANIFEST.json.
-- A `Jurisdiction` is one of Cth, NSW, Vic, Qld, WA, SA, Tas, ACT, NT.
--
-- How to read it.
-- Every rule family is a section.
-- Every function takes a `Jurisdiction` first and answers what that jurisdiction's source module answers.
-- Where the nine agree, one body serves them all.
-- Where they differ, each jurisdiction has its own branch, and the comment on the branch names the source module and its function.
-- A jurisdiction whose source module does not encode a rule family answers NOTHING for it.
-- Nothing is added that a source module does not compute.
--
-- What the caller supplies.
-- Public holidays, bank holidays and days an office is closed are never built in; they are a `Days of rest and closure` the caller passes in.
-- Saturday and Sunday are computed.
-- Sitting days of a House, and the day a letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post, are inputs.
--
-- This file describes what each source module computes.
-- It does not assess the Acts.
-- NOTES (au-time-rules.NOTES.md) lists, family by family and jurisdiction by jurisdiction, what is carried and what is not.

§ `The nouns of this module`

DECLARE Jurisdiction IS ONE OF Cth, NSW, Vic, Qld, WA, SA, Tas, ACT, NT

-- The units a period can be counted in.
-- `Calendar years` is the unit NSW and ACT name separately from a year of 12 months.
DECLARE `Unit of a period` IS ONE OF Days, Weeks, Months, Years, `Calendar years`

-- The ways the nine source modules describe how a period is tied to a day.
-- Each jurisdiction answers only the expressions its own module encodes; the table is in NOTES.
DECLARE `How a period is expressed` IS ONE OF
    `between two days`
    `begins at, on or with a specified day`
    `begins from a specified day`
    `begins after a specified day`
    `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event`
    `continues until a specified day`
    `ends at, on or with a specified day`
    `ends before a specified day`
    `is reckoned to a specified day`
    `occurs between two events`

-- SA and NT carry a flag that a public holiday covers only part of a day; the other jurisdictions ignore the flag.
DECLARE `A public holiday` HAS
    `the day of the holiday`         IS A DATE
    `it covers only part of the day` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts about days that the Acts borrow from other instruments.
-- Which lists a jurisdiction reads is set out in NOTES.
DECLARE `Days of rest and closure` HAS
    `public holidays`                            IS A LIST OF `A public holiday`
    `bank holidays`                              IS A LIST OF DATE
    `public service holidays`                    IS A LIST OF DATE
    `days the office is closed for the whole day` IS A LIST OF DATE

-- What is to be done matters to Qld (filing or registering) and to ACT (office, ordinary, deposit-taking institution).
DECLARE `What is to be done` IS ONE OF
    `filing or registering a document`
    `something at an office of a public entity`
    `anything else`
    `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution`

DECLARE `Point in a day` IS ONE OF
    `the beginning of the day`
    `the last moment of the day`
    `midnight at the end of the day`

DECLARE `Moment in a day` HAS
    `the day of the moment` IS A DATE
    `the point in that day` IS A `Point in a day`

§ `Small helpers`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a whole number of at least 1` n MEANS
    n AT LEAST 1 AND FLOOR n EQUALS n

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF `A public holiday`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d holidays MEANS
    any (GIVEN h YIELD h's `the day of the holiday` EQUALS d) holidays

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      holidays IS A LIST OF `A public holiday`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a public holiday that covers the whole day` d holidays MEANS
    any (GIVEN h YIELD h's `the day of the holiday` EQUALS d AND (NOT h's `it covers only part of the day`)) holidays

-- Sunday, by the day number, as Tas writes it (tas-interpretation-time: `s 29(3): a day is a Sunday`).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Sunday` d MEANS
    ((Day d) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0

§ `Which expression a period is tied to a day by (Cth s 36(1) table; NSW s 36(1); Vic s 44(1) and (2); Qld s 38(1); WA s 61(1); SA s 44(1) table; Tas s 29(1); ACT s 151 table 151; NT s 28(1) and (1A))`

-- Does a period expressed in this way include the specified day?
-- NOTHING where the jurisdiction's module has no rule for that expression.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` (Cth s 36(1) items 1 to 7).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(1) the first day counted in a period dating from a given day` (the given day is left out).
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (the given day is left out).
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the first day of a period` (s 61(1)(a), (b)) with `the end of a period expressed to end on` (s 61(1)(d)) and `the time within a time before a day` (s 61(1)(c)).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1): the first day counted in a period` and `s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7`, with item 1.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): a day is counted in a period of days reckoned forwards from` (the given day is left out).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` j how MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` (Cth s 36(1) items 1 to 7).
    WHEN Cth THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `between two days` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(1) the first day counted in a period dating from a given day` (the given day is left out).
    WHEN NSW THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(1)-(2) the day a period is expressed to begin on or end on is counted in the period`.
    WHEN Vic THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `is reckoned to a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `a day is counted in a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (the given day is left out).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the first day of a period` (s 61(1)(a), (b)) with `the end of a period expressed to end on` (s 61(1)(d)) and `the time within a time before a day` (s 61(1)(c)).
    WHEN WA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1): the first day counted in a period` and `s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7`, with item 1.
    WHEN SA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `between two days` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): a day is counted in a period of days reckoned forwards from` (the given day is left out).
    WHEN Tas THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day`.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `occurs between two events` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period`.
    WHEN NT THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN JUST FALSE
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Does the specified day name the START of a period expressed in this way, for the purpose of counting forward from it?
-- Cth: `the specified day names the start of a period expressed in this way`.
-- The other jurisdictions have no such function; the set below is the expressions their forward-counting functions accept.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the specified day names the start of a period expressed in this way` j how MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: `the specified day names the start of a period expressed in this way`.
    WHEN Cth THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `between two days` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36 the last day of a period of n units dating from a given day` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN NSW THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44 last day counted forward from a day` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN Vic THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `reckon a period` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN WA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1): the last day of a period` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN SA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): the last day of a period of days reckoned forwards from` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN Tas THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN ACT THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins at, on or with a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins after a specified day` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (the expressions that function takes; the map is in the NOTES).
    WHEN NT THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `begins from a specified day` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `begins on, from or after the happening of an act or event` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The first day counted in a period tied to a day by the expression: the specified day, or the day after it.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
      anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day counted in a period` j how anchor MEANS
    IF `the specified day names the start of a period expressed in this way` j how
    THEN CONSIDER `a period expressed in this way includes the specified day` j how
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST anchor
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (anchor PLUS 1)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The last day of a period whose END is tied to a day by the expression.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day of the period`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day`.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the end of a period expressed to end on` (the last day by the calendar).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7: the last day of a period that ends by reference to a specified day`.
-- NSW, Qld, Tas, ACT, NT: no such function in the source module.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
      anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of a period that ends by reference to a day` j how anchor MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day of the period`.
    WHEN Cth THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `between two days` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS 1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(2) last day of a period expressed to end on or be reckoned to a day`.
    WHEN Vic THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `is reckoned to a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Qld: no such rule in qld-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the end of a period expressed to end on` (the last day by the calendar).
    WHEN WA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1) items 4, 5 and 7: the last day of a period that ends by reference to a specified day`.
    WHEN SA THEN
        CONSIDER how
        WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST anchor
        WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS 1)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: no such rule in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

-- The first day of a period of a number of days that ENDS by reference to a day.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))`, read for `ends before a specified day`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): the first day of a period of days reckoned backwards from`, read for `ends before a specified day`.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the time within a time before a day` (s 61(1)(c)).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on`.
-- Cth, NSW, Vic, SA: no such function in the source module.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      n IS A NUMBER
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
      anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day of a period of days that ends by reference to a day` j n how anchor MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the earliest day of a period of days calculated backwards from a given day (s 38(1) and (3))`, read for `ends before a specified day`.
    WHEN Qld THEN
        IF how EQUALS `ends before a specified day` AND n AT LEAST 1 THEN JUST (anchor MINUS n) ELSE NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the time within a time before a day` (s 61(1)(c)).
    WHEN WA THEN
        IF how EQUALS `ends before a specified day` AND `is a whole number of at least 1` n THEN JUST (anchor MINUS n) ELSE NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): the first day of a period of days reckoned backwards from`, read for `ends before a specified day`.
    WHEN Tas THEN
        IF how EQUALS `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS n) ELSE NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151: the first day of a period of days that ends at, by, on or with, or before, a stated day`.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        IF n LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
        ELSE CONSIDER how
             WHEN `continues until a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS (n MINUS 1))
             WHEN `ends at, on or with a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS (n MINUS 1))
             WHEN `ends before a specified day` THEN JUST (anchor MINUS n)
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on`.
    WHEN NT THEN
        IF how EQUALS `ends at, on or with a specified day` AND `is a whole number of at least 1` n
        THEN JUST (anchor PLUS (1 MINUS n))
        ELSE NOTHING

§ `Calendar months and years: the ways the source modules count them (Cth s 2G; NSW Sch 4 "calendar month"; Vic s 44(6); Qld Sch 1 "calendar month"; WA s 62; SA s 4 "month" and "year"; Tas s 46; ACT dictionary "month"; NT s 17)`

-- Counted straight to the corresponding day of the month that many months on.
-- The last day is the day before that corresponding day, or the end of that month if it has no such day.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day of n calendar months starting on` (s 2G(1), (2)).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4 and s 44(1) item 8: the last day of a period of months beginning on a day`.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      s IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of months counted straight to the corresponding day` n s MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY s AT MOST `Days in month` targetMonth targetYear
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY s) targetMonth targetYear MINUS 1
    ELSE Date (`Days in month` targetMonth targetYear) targetMonth targetYear
    WHERE
        monthCount MEANS ((DATE_YEAR s) TIMES 12) PLUS ((DATE_MONTH s) MINUS 1) PLUS n
        targetYear MEANS FLOOR (monthCount DIVIDED BY 12)
        targetMonth MEANS (monthCount MODULO 12) PLUS 1

-- WA counts a period of months with the library's `add months`, which clamps to the end of a short month.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the last day of a period of months beginning on` (s 62(2), (3)).
GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      numberOfMonths IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of months counted with add months` firstDay numberOfMonths MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY target EQUALS DATE_DAY firstDay
    THEN Date (Day target MINUS 1)
    ELSE target
    WHERE
        target MEANS `add months` firstDay numberOfMonths

-- One calendar month at a time: each month starts the day after the one before it ended.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `Schedule 4 the last day of n successive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of a day`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of calendar months in succession`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `dictionary, month: the last day of a run of successive months, the first beginning at the start of a day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "month": the last day of consecutive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of`.
GIVEN s IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of one calendar month starting on` s MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY s AT MOST `Days in month` nextMonth nextYear
    THEN (Date (DATE_DAY s) nextMonth nextYear) MINUS 1
    ELSE Date (`Days in month` nextMonth nextYear) nextMonth nextYear
    WHERE
        nextMonth MEANS IF DATE_MONTH s EQUALS 12 THEN 1 ELSE DATE_MONTH s PLUS 1
        nextYear MEANS IF DATE_MONTH s EQUALS 12 THEN DATE_YEAR s PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR s

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      s IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` n s MEANS
    IF   n AT MOST 1
    THEN `the last day of one calendar month starting on` s
    ELSE `the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (n MINUS 1) ((`the last day of one calendar month starting on` s) PLUS 1)

-- Vic gives an answer for a period of months only where two readings of the text agree.
-- Reading A leaves the given day out and takes the day before the same-numbered day n months on from the next day.
-- Reading B takes the day with the given day's own number, n months on.
-- Each reading is NOTHING where the later month has no day with the number it needs.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(1),(6)(b) last day of n calendar months reckoned from a day` (readings A and B inside it).
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of months where Vic's two readings agree` anchor n MEANS
    CONSIDER readingA
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER readingB
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST b THEN IF a EQUALS b THEN JUST a ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        firstCounted MEANS anchor PLUS 1
        targetA MEANS Date (DATE_DAY firstCounted) (DATE_MONTH firstCounted PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR firstCounted)
        readingA MEANS IF DATE_DAY targetA EQUALS DATE_DAY firstCounted THEN JUST (targetA MINUS 1) ELSE NOTHING
        targetB MEANS Date (DATE_DAY anchor) (DATE_MONTH anchor PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR anchor)
        readingB MEANS IF DATE_DAY targetB EQUALS DATE_DAY anchor THEN JUST targetB ELSE NOTHING

-- Tas counts the same-numbered day in the month reached, and answers NOTHING where that month has no such day.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 46: the day of the same number in the month reached by counting calendar months from`.
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the same-numbered day in the month reached` start months MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY start AT MOST `Days in month` targetMonth targetYear
    THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY start) targetMonth targetYear)
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        monthIndex MEANS ((DATE_YEAR start) TIMES 12) PLUS ((DATE_MONTH start) MINUS 1) PLUS months
        targetYear MEANS FLOOR (monthIndex DIVIDED BY 12)
        targetMonth MEANS (monthIndex MODULO 12) PLUS 1

-- SA counts a year as ending the day before the corresponding day of the next calendar year; a year starting on 29 February ends on 28 February.
-- A period of several years is that many years in succession.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: the last day of a year beginning on a day` and `s 4: the last day of a period of years beginning on a day`.
GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of one year beginning on` firstDay MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY firstDay EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH firstDay EQUALS 2
    THEN Date 28 2 (DATE_YEAR firstDay PLUS 1)
    ELSE (Date (DATE_DAY firstDay) (DATE_MONTH firstDay) (DATE_YEAR firstDay PLUS 1)) MINUS 1

GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      numberOfYears IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of years counted one year at a time` firstDay numberOfYears MEANS
    IF numberOfYears AT MOST 1
    THEN `the last day of one year beginning on` firstDay
    ELSE `the last day of years counted one year at a time` ((`the last day of one year beginning on` firstDay) PLUS 1) (numberOfYears MINUS 1)

§ `The last day of a period of days, months or years (Cth s 36(1) with s 2G; NSW s 36(1) and Sch 4; Vic s 44(1); Qld s 38(1); WA ss 61, 62; SA s 44(1); Tas s 29(1) and s 46; ACT s 151 and dictionary; NT s 28(1))`

-- The last day of a period of n units tied to a day by the expression.
-- The first day is found as above; Vic, Tas and the other modules that start from the given day itself are read from the day before the first day counted.
-- Weeks answer NOTHING for every jurisdiction: the source modules that mention a period of weeks return NOTHING for it.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day of a counted period of` (s 36(1) with s 2G); years answer NOTHING there.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36 the last day of a period of n units dating from a given day`; a year answers NOTHING, a calendar year only from 1 January.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44 last day counted forward from a day` with `s44 last day, start left out`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))`.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `reckon a period` (the last day by the calendar).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1): the last day of a period`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): the last day of a period of days reckoned forwards from`, `s 29(1) and s 46: the last day of a period of calendar months reckoned forwards from`; years and weeks answer NOTHING there.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      n IS A NUMBER
      unit IS A `Unit of a period`
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
      anchor IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of a period` j n unit how anchor MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first day counted in a period` j how anchor
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST first THEN
        CONSIDER j
        -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day of a counted period of` (s 36(1) with s 2G); years answer NOTHING there.
        WHEN Cth THEN
            IF NOT (`is a whole number of at least 1` n) THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (first PLUS (n MINUS 1))
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted straight to the corresponding day` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36 the last day of a period of n units dating from a given day`; a year answers NOTHING, a calendar year only from 1 January.
        WHEN NSW THEN
            IF NOT (`is a whole number of at least 1` n) THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (first PLUS (n MINUS 1))
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN
                     IF DATE_DAY first EQUALS 1 AND DATE_MONTH first EQUALS 1
                     THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (12 TIMES n) first)
                     ELSE NOTHING
        -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44 last day counted forward from a day` with `s44 last day, start left out`.
        WHEN Vic THEN
            CONSIDER unit
            WHEN Days THEN JUST (anchor PLUS n)
            WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
            WHEN Months THEN `the last day of months where Vic's two readings agree` anchor n
            WHEN Years THEN `the last day of months where Vic's two readings agree` anchor (n TIMES 12)
            WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of a period beginning on a given day (s 38(1))`.
        WHEN Qld THEN
            IF n LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (anchor PLUS n)
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (12 TIMES n) first)
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `reckon a period` (the last day by the calendar).
        WHEN WA THEN
            IF NOT (`is a whole number of at least 1` n) THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (first PLUS (n MINUS 1))
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted with add months` first n)
                 WHEN Years THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted with add months` first (n TIMES 12))
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(1): the last day of a period`.
        WHEN SA THEN
            IF n LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (first PLUS (n MINUS 1))
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted straight to the corresponding day` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN JUST (`the last day of years counted one year at a time` first n)
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(1): the last day of a period of days reckoned forwards from`, `s 29(1) and s 46: the last day of a period of calendar months reckoned forwards from`; years and weeks answer NOTHING there.
        WHEN Tas THEN
            CONSIDER unit
            WHEN Days THEN JUST (anchor PLUS n)
            WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
            WHEN Months THEN `the same-numbered day in the month reached` anchor n
            WHEN Years THEN NOTHING
            WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING
        -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day`.
        WHEN ACT THEN
            IF n LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (first PLUS (n MINUS 1))
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN
                     IF DATE_MONTH first EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY first EQUALS 1
                     THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (n TIMES 12) first)
                     ELSE NOTHING
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN
                     IF DATE_MONTH first EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY first EQUALS 1
                     THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (n TIMES 12) first)
                     ELSE NOTHING
        -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from`.
        WHEN NT THEN
            IF NOT (`is a whole number of at least 1` n) THEN NOTHING
            ELSE CONSIDER unit
                 WHEN Days THEN JUST (anchor PLUS n)
                 WHEN Weeks THEN NOTHING
                 WHEN Months THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` n first)
                 WHEN Years THEN JUST (`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` (12 TIMES n) first)
                 WHEN `Calendar years` THEN NOTHING

§ `Days of rest, and the day a thing may be done when its last day is one (Cth s 36(2) and (3); NSW s 36(2); Vic s 44(3) and (4); Qld s 38(2), (3) and (5); WA s 61(1)(e) and (2); SA s 44(2); Tas s 29(3) to (6); ACT s 151A; NT s 28(2))`

-- Only Qld and ACT read the kind of thing; the other jurisdictions ignore it.
-- Qld has a rule for filing or registering and for anything else; ACT for an office of a public entity, anything else, and anything else by a deposit-taking institution.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the jurisdiction states a rule for this kind of thing` j kind MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN Cth THEN TRUE
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(2) the day is a Saturday, a Sunday, or a public holiday or bank holiday in the place` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN NSW THEN TRUE
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(4) a day is a holiday` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN Vic THEN TRUE
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `is an excluded day (s 38(5))` reads the kind of thing: it states a rule for filing or registering a document and for anything else.
    WHEN Qld THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `filing or registering a document` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `something at an office of a public entity` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `anything else` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` THEN FALSE
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `is an excluded day` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN WA THEN TRUE
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: is a business day` (negated) takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN SA THEN TRUE
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3): a day is an excluded day` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN Tas THEN TRUE
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` reads the kind of thing: it states a rule for an office of a public entity, for anything else, and for anything else by a deposit-taking institution.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `filing or registering a document` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `something at an office of a public entity` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anything else` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` THEN TRUE
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` takes no kind of thing, so the rule applies to every kind.
    WHEN NT THEN TRUE

-- Is the day a day of rest for the time for doing a thing?
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` (public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(2) the day is a Saturday, a Sunday, or a public holiday or bank holiday in the place`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(4) a day is a holiday`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `is an excluded day (s 38(5))`: for filing or registering, only a day the office is closed; otherwise a day that is not a business day.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `is an excluded day` (public service holidays, bank holidays and public holidays).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: is a business day` negated: Saturday, Sunday or a public holiday that covers the whole day.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3): a day is an excluded day`: Sunday or a listed holiday; Saturday is not one.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` negated.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a day of rest` j kind d rest MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `is a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday` (public holidays and days the office is closed for the whole day).
    WHEN Cth THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
         OR elem d (rest's `days the office is closed for the whole day`)
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(2) the day is a Saturday, a Sunday, or a public holiday or bank holiday in the place`.
    WHEN NSW THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
         OR elem d (rest's `bank holidays`)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(4) a day is a holiday`.
    WHEN Vic THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `is an excluded day (s 38(5))`: for filing or registering, only a day the office is closed; otherwise a day that is not a business day.
    WHEN Qld THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `filing or registering a document` THEN elem d (rest's `days the office is closed for the whole day`)
        OTHERWISE
                `is weekend` d
             OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
             OR elem d (rest's `bank holidays`)
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `is an excluded day` (public service holidays, bank holidays and public holidays).
    WHEN WA THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR elem d (rest's `public service holidays`)
         OR elem d (rest's `bank holidays`)
         OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: is a business day` negated: Saturday, Sunday or a public holiday that covers the whole day.
    WHEN SA THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR `is a public holiday that covers the whole day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3): a day is an excluded day`: Sunday or a listed holiday; Saturday is not one.
    WHEN Tas THEN
            `is a Sunday` d
         OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` negated.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `something at an office of a public entity` THEN elem d (rest's `days the office is closed for the whole day`)
        WHEN `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` THEN
                `is weekend` d
             OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
             OR elem d (rest's `bank holidays`)
        OTHERWISE
                `is weekend` d
             OR `is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`)
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday`.
    WHEN NT THEN
            `is weekend` d
         OR `is a public holiday that covers the whole day` d (rest's `public holidays`)

-- The first day from a given day, counting the day itself, that is not a day of rest; unbounded search.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` j kind d rest MEANS
    IF   `is a day of rest` j kind d rest
    THEN `the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` j kind (d PLUS 1) rest
    ELSE d

-- Vic searches forward with a limit of 400 days.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(3) first day on or after a day that is not a holiday` and `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends`.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      fuel IS A NUMBER
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Vic: the first day from a day that is not a holiday, within a limit on the search` d fuel rest MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF fuel AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        IF `is a day of rest` Vic `anything else` d rest THEN `Vic: the first day from a day that is not a holiday, within a limit on the search` (d PLUS 1) (fuel MINUS 1) rest
        OTHERWISE JUST d

-- ACT searches forward with a limit of 400 days, starting at the last day itself.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (2): the first working day on or after a day, searching a limited number of days`.
GIVEN kind IS A `What is to be done`
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
      left IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ACT: the first working day from a day, within a limit on the search` kind d rest left MEANS
    IF   NOT (`is a day of rest` ACT kind d rest)
    THEN JUST d
    ELSE IF   left AT MOST 0
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE `ACT: the first working day from a day, within a limit on the search` kind (d PLUS 1) rest (left MINUS 1)

-- The latest day on which a thing may be done when the last day for doing it is the given day.
-- Seven jurisdictions step forward to the first day that is not a day of rest; Vic and ACT do so with a limit of 400 days.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day on which the thing may be done` (with an Act that requires or allows the thing taken as true).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(2) the latest day on which the thing may be done when the period ends on a day`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (with the time limited for doing an act taken as true).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))`.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the next day that is not an excluded day, counting the day itself`.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(2): the last day on which a thing may be done`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3)(a): the last day on which an act is in due time, a time reckoned forwards ending on`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      lastDay IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest day on which a thing may be done` j kind lastDay rest MEANS
    IF NOT (`the jurisdiction states a rule for this kind of thing` j kind)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER j
         -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the last day on which the thing may be done` (with an Act that requires or allows the thing taken as true).
         WHEN Cth THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` Cth kind lastDay rest)
         -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(2) the latest day on which the thing may be done when the period ends on a day`.
         WHEN NSW THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` NSW kind lastDay rest)
         -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(3) day to which a time limited for doing an act or thing extends` (with the time limited for doing an act taken as true).
         WHEN Vic THEN
             IF `is a day of rest` Vic kind lastDay rest
             THEN `Vic: the first day from a day that is not a holiday, within a limit on the search` (lastDay PLUS 1) 400 rest
             ELSE JUST lastDay
         -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a time or last day calculated forwards is taken to fall on (s 38(2))`.
         WHEN Qld THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` Qld kind lastDay rest)
         -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the next day that is not an excluded day, counting the day itself`.
         WHEN WA THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` WA kind lastDay rest)
         -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 44(2): the last day on which a thing may be done`.
         WHEN SA THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` SA kind lastDay rest)
         -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3)(a): the last day on which an act is in due time, a time reckoned forwards ending on`.
         WHEN Tas THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` Tas kind lastDay rest)
         -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151A (2): the day on which the thing must or may be done, where the particular day or the last day of the period is that day`.
         WHEN ACT THEN `ACT: the first working day from a day, within a limit on the search` kind lastDay rest 400
         -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is`.
         WHEN NT THEN JUST (`the first day from a day that is not a day of rest` NT kind lastDay rest)

-- The day a time, or earliest day, calculated BACKWARDS is taken to fall on: the first earlier day that is not a day of rest.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3)(b): the day on or before which an act is in due time, a time reckoned backwards ending on`.
-- The other seven source modules have no backward rule.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day a time calculated backwards is taken to fall on` j kind d rest MEANS
    IF NOT (`the jurisdiction states a rule for this kind of thing` j kind)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER j
         -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
         -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
         -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
         -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a time or earliest day calculated backwards is taken to fall on (s 38(3))`.
         WHEN Qld THEN JUST (`the first earlier day that is not a day of rest` Qld kind d rest)
         -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
         -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
         -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(3)(b): the day on or before which an act is in due time, a time reckoned backwards ending on`.
         WHEN Tas THEN JUST (`the first earlier day that is not a day of rest` Tas kind d rest)
         -- ACT: no such rule in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
         -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
         WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first earlier day that is not a day of rest` j kind d rest MEANS
    IF   `is a day of rest` j kind d rest
    THEN `the first earlier day that is not a day of rest` j kind (d MINUS 1) rest
    ELSE d

-- Tas counts a time of 6 days or fewer without reckoning days of rest.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(6): the day reached by counting days forwards from a day, excluded days not reckoned`.
GIVEN start IS A DATE
      remaining IS A NUMBER
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A DATE
`Tas: the day reached counting days forwards, days of rest not reckoned` start remaining rest MEANS
    IF remaining AT MOST 0
    THEN start
    ELSE IF `is a day of rest` Tas `anything else` (start PLUS 1) rest
         THEN `Tas: the day reached counting days forwards, days of rest not reckoned` (start PLUS 1) remaining rest
         ELSE `Tas: the day reached counting days forwards, days of rest not reckoned` (start PLUS 1) (remaining MINUS 1) rest

-- The latest day on which a thing may be done within a period: the last day of the period, then the day-of-rest rule.
-- Tas applies s 29(6) instead when the period is 1 to 6 days.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29: the last day for doing an act within a number of days reckoned forwards from`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      kind IS A `What is to be done`
      n IS A NUMBER
      unit IS A `Unit of a period`
      how IS A `How a period is expressed`
      anchor IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest day on which a thing may be done within a period` j kind n unit how anchor rest MEANS
    IF   j EQUALS Tas AND unit EQUALS Days AND n AT LEAST 1 AND n AT MOST 6
    THEN IF `the specified day names the start of a period expressed in this way` Tas how
         THEN JUST (`Tas: the day reached counting days forwards, days of rest not reckoned` anchor n rest)
         ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the last day of a period` j n unit how anchor
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST last THEN `the latest day on which a thing may be done` j kind last rest

§ `Business days (Cth s 2B; NSW Sch 4 and s 76(2); Qld Sch 1; SA s 4; ACT dictionary; NT s 17)`

-- Is the day a business day?
-- Vic, WA and Tas have no definition of a business day in their source modules.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `is a business day` (not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday in the place concerned; days an office is closed are not read).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `Schedule 4 the day is a business day` and `s 76(2) the day is a working day` (public and bank holidays).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (public, special and bank holidays).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: is a business day` (a part-day public holiday does not count).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `dictionary, business day: the day is a business day` (public and bank holidays).
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (a part-day public holiday does not count).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      d IS A DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`is a business day` j d rest MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `is a business day` (not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday in the place concerned; days an office is closed are not read).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST ((NOT (`is weekend` d)) AND (NOT (`is a public holiday, whether or not it covers only part of the day` d (rest's `public holidays`))))
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `Schedule 4 the day is a business day` and `s 76(2) the day is a working day` (public and bank holidays).
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (NOT (`is a day of rest` NSW `anything else` d rest))
    -- Vic: no definition of a business day in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `is a business day (Schedule 1)` (public, special and bank holidays).
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (NOT (`is a day of rest` Qld `anything else` d rest))
    -- WA: no definition of a business day in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: is a business day` (a part-day public holiday does not count).
    WHEN SA THEN JUST (NOT (`is a day of rest` SA `anything else` d rest))
    -- Tas: no definition of a business day in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `dictionary, business day: the day is a business day` (public and bank holidays).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (NOT (`is a day of rest` ACT `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` d rest))
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (a part-day public holiday does not count).
    WHEN NT THEN JUST (NOT (`is a day of rest` NT `anything else` d rest))

§ `When an enactment begins and stops operating, and at what moment of the day (Cth ss 3 and 3A; NSW ss 23, 24, 71 and Sch 4; Vic ss 11, 12, 24, 25 and 44(6)(a); Qld ss 15A, 15B, 18 and Sch 1; WA ss 20, 21; SA ss 27, 28, 30; Tas ss 9, 14, 16; ACT ss 73, 74, 85; NT ss 5, 6A)`

-- An enactment that comes into operation on a particular day does so at the beginning of that day.
-- All nine source modules say so.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the moment the enactment comes into operation` (s 3).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 24 the moment an Act or statutory rule commences on a particular day` (an Act or a statutory rule; another instrument is NOTHING there and is not reproduced here).
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (s 11(1)) and `s24 moment a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule comes into operation`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)`.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the moment a written law comes into operation` (s 21).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 28: the moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a particular day`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 9(5): the moment at which an Act or instrument expressed to commence on a day takes effect`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (s 74: unless a different time is provided).
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 6A: the moment at which an Act or a provision commences` (unless a time of day is provided in the Act).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment in a day`
`the moment an enactment comes into operation on a day` j d MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the moment the enactment comes into operation` (s 3).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 24 the moment an Act or statutory rule commences on a particular day` (an Act or a statutory rule; another instrument is NOTHING there and is not reproduced here).
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s11 moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a fixed day` (s 11(1)) and `s24 moment a subordinate instrument that is not a statutory rule comes into operation`.
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the moment a provision commences on a day (s 15B)`.
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the moment a written law comes into operation` (s 21).
    WHEN WA THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 28: the moment an Act or provision comes into operation on a particular day`.
    WHEN SA THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 9(5): the moment at which an Act or instrument expressed to commence on a day takes effect`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` (s 74: unless a different time is provided).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 6A: the moment at which an Act or a provision commences` (unless a time of day is provided in the Act).
    WHEN NT THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the beginning of the day`)

-- The moment up to which an enactment expressed to expire on a day, or to continue in force until a day, has effect.
-- NSW, Qld, SA and ACT name the end of the day, as midnight; Vic and Tas name the last moment of the day.
-- Cth, WA and NT: no such rule in the source module.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 71 the moment an Act or instrument expressed to expire or remain in force until a day stops operating`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s12 moment until which a temporary Act or provision continues in operation`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)`.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 30: the moment up to which an expiring provision continues to have effect`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 14(2): the last moment of operation of an enactment expressed to expire or remain in force until a specified day`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect`, for a law not remade on that day (the repeal takes effect at midnight on the day).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment in a day`
`the moment an enactment stops operating on its expiry day` j d MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 71 the moment an Act or instrument expressed to expire or remain in force until a day stops operating`.
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s12 moment until which a temporary Act or provision continues in operation`.
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the last moment of the day`)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last moment an Act or provision has effect (s 18)`.
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 30: the moment up to which an expiring provision continues to have effect`.
    WHEN SA THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 14(2): the last moment of operation of an enactment expressed to expire or remain in force until a specified day`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `the last moment of the day`)
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect`, for a law not remade on that day (the repeal takes effect at midnight on the day).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

-- Midnight, in relation to a particular day, is the point at which that day ends.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `Schedule 4 midnight in relation to a particular day`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(a) midnight in relation to a day is the point at which that day ends`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 74 and dictionary, midnight` (midnight at the end of the day).
-- Cth, WA, SA, Tas, NT: no such definition in the source module.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Moment in a day`
`midnight in relation to a day` j d MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `Schedule 4 midnight in relation to a particular day`.
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(a) midnight in relation to a day is the point at which that day ends`.
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `midnight of a day, the point of time at which the day ends (Schedule 1)`.
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 74 and dictionary, midnight` (midnight at the end of the day).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (`Moment in a day` OF d, `midnight at the end of the day`)
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

§ `The day an Act commences when it says nothing about its commencement (Cth s 3A; NSW s 23(1)(a); Qld s 15A; WA s 20; SA s 27(1); ACT s 73(1); NT s 5(4))`

-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the day the enactment commences` (s 3A(2): the 28th day after the day of Royal Assent; an Act to alter the Constitution is not reproduced here).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 23(1)(a) the day an Act commences when nothing else provides` (the day occurring 28 days after assent).
-- Vic: s 10A names a day to be proclaimed or the first anniversary; see the automatic-commencement section below. NOTHING here.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` (the Act does not otherwise expressly provide).
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the day an Act comes into operation` (s 20: assent before 1 July 1984, the day of assent; otherwise the 28th day after).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 27(1): the day an Act with no commencement provision comes into operation`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time s 9(2) and (3) depend on the day section 8 of the 1981 amending Act commenced, which the module takes as an input and this surface does not; NOTHING here.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` (the day after the notification day; the input is read as the notification day).
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (the day after the day assent is declared).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      assent IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an Act that says nothing about its commencement commences` j assent MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the day the enactment commences` (s 3A(2): the 28th day after the day of Royal Assent; an Act to alter the Constitution is not reproduced here).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (assent PLUS 28)
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 23(1)(a) the day an Act commences when nothing else provides` (the day occurring 28 days after assent).
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (assent PLUS 28)
    -- Vic: s 10A names a day to be proclaimed or the first anniversary; see the automatic-commencement section below. NOTHING here.
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day an Act commences on the date of assent (s 15A)` (the Act does not otherwise expressly provide).
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST assent
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the day an Act comes into operation` (s 20: assent before 1 July 1984, the day of assent; otherwise the 28th day after).
    WHEN WA THEN
        IF Day assent LESS THAN Day (Date 1 7 1984)
        THEN JUST assent
        ELSE JUST (assent PLUS 28)
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 27(1): the day an Act with no commencement provision comes into operation`.
    WHEN SA THEN JUST assent
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time s 9(2) and (3) depend on the day section 8 of the 1981 amending Act commenced, which the module takes as an input and this surface does not; NOTHING here.
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` (the day after the notification day; the input is read as the notification day).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (assent PLUS 1)
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (the day after the day assent is declared).
    WHEN NT THEN JUST (assent PLUS 1)

§ `A day fixed for commencement that is not later than the day the proclamation or notice is published (NSW s 23(5); Vic s 11(2A); Qld s 15D; ACT s 77(3) and (4))`

-- Cth, WA, SA, Tas and NT: no such rule in the source module.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 23(1) and (5) the day an Act commences` (a day fixed by proclamation, published later: the later of the two).
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s11 commencement once the proclamation is published` (the proclamation made on or before the fixed day; otherwise NOTHING).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` (the later of the two).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (the day after the notification day, unless the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement under authority given by an Act).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      fixedDay IS A DATE
      publishedDay IS A DATE
      `the proclamation was made on or before the fixed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement and provides for it under authority given by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an Act commences when the day fixed is not later than the day of publication` j fixedDay publishedDay `the proclamation was made on or before the fixed day` `the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement and provides for it under authority given by an Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 23(1) and (5) the day an Act commences` (a day fixed by proclamation, published later: the later of the two).
    WHEN NSW THEN
        IF Day publishedDay AT MOST Day fixedDay THEN JUST fixedDay ELSE JUST publishedDay
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s11 commencement once the proclamation is published` (the proclamation made on or before the fixed day; otherwise NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN
        BRANCH
            IF publishedDay AT MOST fixedDay THEN JUST fixedDay
            IF `the proclamation was made on or before the fixed day` THEN JUST publishedDay
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day an Act commences when a day is fixed by proclamation (s 15D)` (the later of the two).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        IF fixedDay LESS THAN publishedDay THEN JUST publishedDay ELSE JUST fixedDay
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice` (the day after the notification day, unless the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement under authority given by an Act).
    WHEN ACT THEN
        IF   fixedDay AT MOST publishedDay
         AND NOT `the notice clearly indicates an earlier commencement and provides for it under authority given by an Act`
        THEN JUST (publishedDay PLUS 1)
        ELSE JUST fixedDay
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

§ `An Act to commence on a day to be fixed that has not commenced by a time limit (Vic s 10A(3) and (4); Qld s 15DA; SA s 27(6) and (7); ACT s 79(1))`

-- The day by which the Act commences automatically if no earlier day has been fixed.
-- Cth, NSW, WA, Tas and NT: no such rule in the source module.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` (NOTHING where the year has no same-numbered day).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)`; the two further inputs are the Act's own statement that s 15DA does not apply and the months a regulation has extended the period to (0 if none).
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 27(6) and (7): the day an Act or provision to be brought into operation by proclamation comes into operation`, with the provision covered by s 27(6), no proclamation made, and the Act's own statement that s 27(6) does not apply.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences`: the first day after 6 months beginning on the notification day (the input is read as the notification day).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      assentOrNotification IS A DATE
      `the Act says that the automatic rule does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an Act to commence on a day to be fixed commences automatically` j assentOrNotification `the Act says that the automatic rule does not apply` `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s10A first anniversary of the passing of an Act` (NOTHING where the year has no same-numbered day).
    WHEN Vic THEN
        IF DATE_DAY vicAnniversary EQUALS DATE_DAY assentOrNotification THEN JUST vicAnniversary ELSE NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the day a postponed law automatically commences (s 15DA)`; the two further inputs are the Act's own statement that s 15DA does not apply and the months a regulation has extended the period to (0 if none).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        IF     assentOrNotification GREATER THAN Date 31 12 1994
           AND (NOT `the Act says that the automatic rule does not apply`)
           AND (   `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` EQUALS 0
                OR (`the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` AT LEAST 13 AND `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` AT MOST 24))
        THEN JUST ((`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` qldMonths (assentOrNotification PLUS 1)) PLUS 1)
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 27(6) and (7): the day an Act or provision to be brought into operation by proclamation comes into operation`, with the provision covered by s 27(6), no proclamation made, and the Act's own statement that s 27(6) does not apply.
    WHEN SA THEN
        IF `the Act says that the automatic rule does not apply` THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF DATE_DAY saAnniversary EQUALS DATE_DAY assentOrNotification AND DATE_MONTH saAnniversary EQUALS DATE_MONTH assentOrNotification
             THEN JUST saAnniversary
             ELSE NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences`: the first day after 6 months beginning on the notification day (the input is read as the notification day).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST ((`the last day of months counted one calendar month at a time` 6 assentOrNotification) PLUS 1)
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        vicAnniversary MEANS Date (DATE_DAY assentOrNotification) (DATE_MONTH assentOrNotification) (DATE_YEAR assentOrNotification PLUS 1)
        saAnniversary MEANS Date (DATE_DAY assentOrNotification) (DATE_MONTH assentOrNotification) (DATE_YEAR assentOrNotification PLUS 2)
        qldMonths MEANS IF `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none` EQUALS 0 THEN 12 ELSE `the months a regulation has extended the period to, or 0 if none`

§ `When an amending Act is repealed automatically (NSW s 30C(2) and (3); Qld s 22C(1); ACT s 89(1))`

-- The day on which an amending Act is repealed once all its provisions have commenced.
-- Cth, Vic, WA, SA, Tas and NT: no such rule in the source module.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 30C(2) and (3) the day an amending Act is repealed` (the day after the last commencement, or the day after assent if the last commencement is before assent).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (an amending Act enacted after 30 June 1994; the module's own flag that the Act is an amending Act is taken as true); read at the day it falls on.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` (all provisions commenced; the alternative limb of paragraph (b) is not read).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      assent IS A DATE
      `the day on which the last provision commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day an amending Act is repealed automatically` j assent `the day on which the last provision commenced` MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 30C(2) and (3) the day an amending Act is repealed` (the day after the last commencement, or the day after assent if the last commencement is before assent).
    WHEN NSW THEN
        IF Day `the day on which the last provision commenced` LESS THAN Day assent
        THEN JUST (assent PLUS 1)
        ELSE JUST (`the day on which the last provision commenced` PLUS 1)
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the moment an amending Act is automatically repealed (s 22C(1))` (an amending Act enacted after 30 June 1994; the module's own flag that the Act is an amending Act is taken as true); read at the day it falls on.
    WHEN Qld THEN
        IF assent GREATER THAN Date 30 6 1994 THEN JUST (`the day on which the last provision commenced` PLUS 1) ELSE NOTHING
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` (all provisions commenced; the alternative limb of paragraph (b) is not read).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (`the day on which the last provision commenced` PLUS 1)
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

§ `The day a person attains an age, and a person's age on a day (Cth s 37A; NSW s 37; Vic s 55(2); Qld s 38A; SA s 49; ACT s 149; NT s 30)`

-- The day on which a person attains an age expressed in years.
-- WA, Tas and Qld give no such day: WA and Tas have no age rule, and Qld computes an age on a day (next function).
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the moment a person attains the age` (s 37A: NOTHING where that year has no anniversary day; the day of the moment is returned).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 37 the moment a person attains an age in years` (the day of the moment is returned).
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s55(2) day on which a person born on a day reaches eighteen years, taken as the eighteenth anniversary`; the module encodes eighteen years only, so any other age is NOTHING.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 49: the moment a person attains an age in years` (1 March in a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February; the day of the moment is returned).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` (28 February in a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      born IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day a person attains an age in years` j born years MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the moment a person attains the age` (s 37A: NOTHING where that year has no anniversary day; the day of the moment is returned).
    WHEN Cth THEN
        IF years LESS THAN 1 OR (NOT (FLOOR years EQUALS years))
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF DATE_DAY born AT MOST `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear
             THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear)
             ELSE NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 37 the moment a person attains an age in years` (the day of the moment is returned).
    WHEN NSW THEN
        IF years AT LEAST 0 AND FLOOR years EQUALS years
        THEN IF DATE_DAY born EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH born EQUALS 2 AND NOT (`is leap year` anniversaryYear)
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear)
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s55(2) day on which a person born on a day reaches eighteen years, taken as the eighteenth anniversary`; the module encodes eighteen years only, so any other age is NOTHING.
    WHEN Vic THEN
        IF years EQUALS 18 AND DATE_DAY vicTarget EQUALS DATE_DAY born THEN JUST vicTarget ELSE NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time has no day on which an age is attained; it computes an age on a day (`the age in years of a person on a day`) (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: no age rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 49: the moment a person attains an age in years` (1 March in a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February; the day of the moment is returned).
    WHEN SA THEN
        IF DATE_DAY born EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH born EQUALS 2 AND NOT (`is leap year` anniversaryYear)
        THEN JUST (Date 1 3 anniversaryYear)
        ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear)
    -- Tas: no age rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years`.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        IF years LESS THAN 0
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF DATE_DAY born AT MOST `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear
             THEN JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear)
             ELSE NOTHING
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` (28 February in a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February).
    WHEN NT THEN
        IF years LESS THAN 1 OR (NOT (FLOOR years EQUALS years))
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF DATE_DAY born EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH born EQUALS 2 AND (NOT (`is leap year` anniversaryYear))
             THEN JUST (Date 28 2 anniversaryYear)
             ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) anniversaryYear)
    WHERE
        anniversaryYear MEANS DATE_YEAR born PLUS years
        vicTarget MEANS Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) (DATE_YEAR born PLUS 18)

-- A person's age in years on a day.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (NOTHING on 28 February of a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day`.
-- The other seven source modules have no such function.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      born IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the age in years of a person on a day` j born day MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the age in years of a person on a day (s 38A)` (NOTHING on 28 February of a year without 29 February for a person born on 29 February).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        IF day LESS THAN born
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF     DATE_MONTH born EQUALS 2
                AND DATE_DAY born EQUALS 29
                AND (NOT `is leap year` (DATE_YEAR day))
                AND DATE_MONTH day EQUALS 2
                AND DATE_DAY day EQUALS 28
             THEN NOTHING
             ELSE IF ((DATE_MONTH day) TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY day) AT LEAST ((DATE_MONTH born) TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY born)
                  THEN JUST (DATE_YEAR day MINUS DATE_YEAR born)
                  ELSE JUST (DATE_YEAR day MINUS DATE_YEAR born MINUS 1)
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day`.
    WHEN ACT THEN
        IF day LESS THAN born
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE IF DATE_DAY born AT MOST `Days in month` (DATE_MONTH born) (DATE_YEAR day)
             THEN JUST (yearsApart MINUS (IF day LESS THAN Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) (DATE_YEAR day) THEN 1 ELSE 0))
             ELSE IF day LESS THAN Date 28 2 (DATE_YEAR day)
                  THEN JUST (yearsApart MINUS 1)
                  ELSE IF day AT LEAST Date 1 3 (DATE_YEAR day)
                       THEN JUST yearsApart
                       ELSE NOTHING
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        yearsApart MEANS DATE_YEAR day MINUS DATE_YEAR born

§ `Service by post (Cth s 29; NSW s 76; Vic s 49; Qld s 39A; WA s 75(1); SA s 51(5); Tas s 30; ACT s 250; NT s 25)`

-- The n-th working day after a day, where a working day is not a day of rest.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 76 the nth working day after a day`.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A DATE
`NSW: the n-th working day after a day` d n rest MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN d
    ELSE IF NOT (`is a day of rest` NSW `anything else` next rest)
         THEN `NSW: the n-th working day after a day` next (n MINUS 1) rest
         ELSE `NSW: the n-th working day after a day` next n rest
    WHERE
        next MEANS d PLUS 1

-- The day service of a document by post is taken to be effected.
-- Inputs: whether the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter (read where the source module reads it);
-- the day it was posted; the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post; and the day service in fact took place if the contrary is proved.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the day service by post is taken to be effected` (s 29(1)): the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 76(1)(b) the day service by post in Australia or an external Territory is taken to be effected` (the seventh working day after posting; the ordinary-course day is not read).
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING where the contrary is proved; the flag is not read).
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING where the contrary is proved; the flag is not read).
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the day service by post is deemed effected` (s 75(1)): the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 51(5): the moment service by post is taken to be effected` (the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; the flag is not read).
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 30(1): the day service by post is deemed to have been effected` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done or the contrary is proved).
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served`, by prepaid post (the ordinary-course day).
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served`, by prepaid post (the ordinary-course day).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      `the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      posted IS A DATE
      `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE
      `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved` IS A MAYBE DATE
      rest IS A `Days of rest and closure`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day service by post is taken to be effected` j `the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter` posted `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved` rest MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the day service by post is taken to be effected` (s 29(1)): the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done.
    WHEN Cth THEN
        IF `the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter`
        THEN CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
             WHEN JUST proved THEN JUST proved
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 76(1)(b) the day service by post in Australia or an external Territory is taken to be effected` (the seventh working day after posting; the ordinary-course day is not read).
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (`NSW: the n-th working day after a day` posted 7 rest)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s49 day on which service by post is deemed effected` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING where the contrary is proved; the flag is not read).
    WHEN Vic THEN
        CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
        WHEN JUST proved THEN NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the time service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b))` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING where the contrary is proved; the flag is not read).
    WHEN Qld THEN
        CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
        WHEN JUST proved THEN NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the day service by post is deemed effected` (s 75(1)): the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done.
    WHEN WA THEN
        IF `the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter`
        THEN CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
             WHEN JUST proved THEN JUST proved
             WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 51(5): the moment service by post is taken to be effected` (the contrary day if proved, otherwise the ordinary-course day; the flag is not read).
    WHEN SA THEN
        CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
        WHEN JUST proved THEN JUST proved
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 30(1): the day service by post is deemed to have been effected` (the ordinary-course day; NOTHING if not properly done or the contrary is proved).
    WHEN Tas THEN
        CONSIDER `the day service in fact took place, if the contrary is proved`
        WHEN JUST proved THEN NOTHING
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            IF `the document was properly addressed, prepaid and posted as a letter`
            THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
            ELSE NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served`, by prepaid post (the ordinary-course day).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served`, by prepaid post (the ordinary-course day).
    WHEN NT THEN JUST `the day it would be delivered in the ordinary course of post`

§ `Sitting days of a House (Cth s 2M; NSW s 18; Tas s 44; NT s 17 "sitting day")`

-- The n-th sitting day after a day, from the days the caller supplies.
-- For Cth the supplied days are the days on which a sitting BEGINS (the later days of a long sitting are part of the earlier sitting day); for NSW, Tas and NT they are the days the House sat or met.
-- Cth, NSW and NT sort the days; Cth and NT also drop repeats; Tas takes the supplied order as it is.
-- Vic, Qld, WA and SA and ACT: no such function in the source module.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the sitting day that is the n-th after` (s 2M with s 36(1) item 6).
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 18 the nth sitting day of a House after a day`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 44: the sitting day of a House that is the number given after a day`.
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after`.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
      sittings IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the n-th sitting day after a day` j n d sittings MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the sitting day that is the n-th after` (s 2M with s 36(1) item 6).
    WHEN Cth THEN
        IF n LESS THAN 1 OR (NOT (FLOOR n EQUALS n)) OR count cthLater LESS THAN n
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (Date (at cthLater (n MINUS 1)))
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 18 the nth sitting day of a House after a day`.
    WHEN NSW THEN
        IF n AT LEAST 1 AND FLOOR n EQUALS n AND count later AT LEAST n
        THEN JUST (Date (at (sort (map (GIVEN x YIELD Day x) later)) (n MINUS 1)))
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: no such rule in qld-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 44: the sitting day of a House that is the number given after a day`.
    WHEN Tas THEN
        IF count later AT LEAST n AND n AT LEAST 1
        THEN JUST (at later (n MINUS 1))
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- ACT: no such rule in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "sitting day": the nth sitting day after`.
    WHEN NT THEN
        IF n LESS THAN 1 OR (NOT (FLOOR n EQUALS n)) OR count cthLater LESS THAN n
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST (Date (at cthLater (n MINUS 1)))
    WHERE
        later MEANS filter (GIVEN x YIELD Day x GREATER THAN Day d) sittings
        cthLater MEANS sort (nub (map (GIVEN x YIELD Day x) later))

§ `Financial years and calendar years (Cth s 2B; NSW Sch 4; Vic s 44(6); Qld Sch 1; WA s 5; SA s 4; Tas s 45(1); ACT dictionary and s 89(2); NT s 17)`

-- Every source module that defines a financial year says it runs from 1 July to 30 June.
-- Every source module that defines a calendar year says it runs from 1 January to 31 December.
-- Which of the four dates each module computes is set out here; the year asked about is the year in which the financial year ENDS, or the calendar year itself.
-- Where a module takes the year in which the financial year BEGINS, the branch comment says so.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the financial year containing` and `the calendar year containing`.
-- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(d) first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of a year`, `s44(6)(d) midnight at which the financial year ending in a calendar year ends`, `s44(6)(e) first day of the calendar year ending on 31 December of a year`, `s44(6)(e) midnight at which a calendar year ends`.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the first day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)`, `the last day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)`, `the last day of the financial year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1)` (taking the year it begins in).
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the first day of the financial year ending in` and `the last day of the financial year ending in`.
-- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: the last day of the calendar year` and `s 4: the last day of the financial year starting on 1 July` (taking the year it starts in).
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 45(1): the first day of the financial year ending in the year` and `s 45(1): the last day of the financial year ending in the year`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 89 (2): the day an appropriation Act is automatically repealed` (the last day of the financial year beginning in the year given).
-- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "financial year": the first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of` and `s 17 "calendar year": the last day of the calendar year of`.
-- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36 the last day of a period of n units dating from a given day` with a calendar year (31 December).
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day of the financial year ending in` j yearOfEnding MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the financial year containing` (a financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June; the first day of the span is returned).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1))
    -- NSW: no financial-year rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(d) first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of a year`.
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1))
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time has `the last day of the financial year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1)` only, with no first-day function (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the first day of the financial year ending in`.
    WHEN WA THEN JUST (Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1))
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time has `s 4: the last day of the financial year starting on 1 July` only, with no first-day function (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 45(1): the first day of the financial year ending in the year`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST (Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1))
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time has `s 89 (2): the day an appropriation Act is automatically repealed` only, with no first-day function (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "financial year": the first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of`.
    WHEN NT THEN JUST (Date 1 7 (yearOfEnding MINUS 1))

GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      yearOfEnding IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the financial year ending in` j yearOfEnding MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the financial year containing` (the last day of the span is returned).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- NSW: no financial-year rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(d) midnight at which the financial year ending in a calendar year ends` (the day of that midnight).
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of the financial year beginning on 1 July (Schedule 1)` (it takes the year the financial year begins in).
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the last day of the financial year ending in`.
    WHEN WA THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: the last day of the financial year starting on 1 July` (it takes the year the financial year starts in).
    WHEN SA THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 45(1): the last day of the financial year ending in the year`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 89 (2): the day an appropriation Act is automatically repealed` (it takes the year the financial year begins in).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (Date 30 6 yearOfEnding)
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time has `s 17 "financial year": the first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of` only, with no last-day function (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the first day of the calendar year` j year MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the calendar year containing` (the first day of the span is returned).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (Date 1 1 year)
    -- NSW: no first-day-of-calendar-year function in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(e) first day of the calendar year ending on 31 December of a year`.
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (Date 1 1 year)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the first day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)`.
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (Date 1 1 year)
    -- WA: no calendar-year function in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no first-day-of-calendar-year function in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no calendar-year function in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: no first-day-of-calendar-year function in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: no first-day-of-calendar-year function in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the calendar year` j year MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the calendar year containing` (the last day of the span is returned).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- NSW: nsw-interpretation-time `s 36(1) and Schedule 4 the last day of a period of n calendar years dating from a given day` (one calendar year dating from 31 December of the year before).
    WHEN NSW THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- Vic: vic-interpretation-time `s44(6)(e) midnight at which a calendar year ends` (the day of that midnight).
    WHEN Vic THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the last day of the calendar year (Schedule 1)`.
    WHEN Qld THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- WA: no calendar-year function in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: sa-interpretation-time `s 4: the last day of the calendar year`.
    WHEN SA THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- Tas: no calendar-year function in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `dictionary, calendar year and year: the last day of a run of calendar years beginning at the start of a day` (one calendar year beginning on 1 January).
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)
    -- NT: nt-interpretation-time `s 17 "calendar year": the last day of the calendar year of`.
    WHEN NT THEN JUST (Date 31 12 year)

-- The calendar year in which the financial year containing a day ends.
-- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the financial year containing` (the year of its last day).
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the calendar year in which the financial year containing the date ends`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 45(1): the year in which the financial year containing a day ends`.
-- The other six source modules have no such function.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the year in which the financial year containing a day ends` j d MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: au-interpretation-time `the financial year containing` (the year of its last day).
    WHEN Cth THEN JUST (IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 7 THEN DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR d)
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: no such rule in qld-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the calendar year in which the financial year containing the date ends`.
    WHEN WA THEN JUST (IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 7 THEN DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR d)
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 45(1): the year in which the financial year containing a day ends`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST (IF DATE_MONTH d AT LEAST 7 THEN DATE_YEAR d PLUS 1 ELSE DATE_YEAR d)
    -- ACT: no such rule in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

§ `Clear days and days between events (Qld s 38(1); Tas s 29(2); WA s 61(1)(f) and (g); ACT s 151 table 151 item 5)`

-- The earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after a number of clear days from a given day.
-- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))`.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(2): the earliest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled after a number of clear days from`.
-- The other seven source modules have no such function.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      n IS A NUMBER
      given IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days` j n given MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: qld-interpretation-time `the earliest day on which the purpose can be fulfilled after clear days (s 38(1)(a))`.
    WHEN Qld THEN IF n LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST ((given PLUS n) PLUS 1)
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(2): the earliest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled after a number of clear days from`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST ((given PLUS n) PLUS 1)
    -- ACT: no such rule in act-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN ACT THEN NOTHING
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

-- The latest day for an event so that a number of clear days lie between it and a later day.
-- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(2): the latest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled before a number of clear days from`.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the latest day for the earlier event, so that the given number of days lie between the 2 events`.
-- The other seven source modules have no such function.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      n IS A NUMBER
      laterDay IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the latest day for the earlier event so that clear days lie between` j n laterDay MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: no such rule in qld-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: no such rule in wa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN WA THEN NOTHING
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: tas-interpretation-time `s 29(2): the latest day on which the purpose may be fulfilled before a number of clear days from`.
    WHEN Tas THEN JUST ((laterDay MINUS n) MINUS 1)
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the latest day for the earlier event, so that the given number of days lie between the 2 events`.
    WHEN ACT THEN JUST (laterDay MINUS (n PLUS 1))
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING

-- The number of days counted between two events.
-- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the number of days counted between two events`: clear days, or at least a number of days, exclude both event days; any other count excludes the first event's day and includes the second's.
-- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the number of days between 2 events` (both event days excluded).
-- The other seven source modules have no such function.
GIVEN j IS A Jurisdiction
      `clear days, or at least a number of days` IS A BOOLEAN
      firstEvent IS A DATE
      secondEvent IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the number of days counted between two events` j `clear days, or at least a number of days` firstEvent secondEvent MEANS
    CONSIDER j
    -- Cth: no such rule in au-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Cth THEN NOTHING
    -- NSW: no such rule in nsw-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NSW THEN NOTHING
    -- Vic: no such rule in vic-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Vic THEN NOTHING
    -- Qld: no such rule in qld-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Qld THEN NOTHING
    -- WA: wa-interpretation-time `the number of days counted between two events`: clear days, or at least a number of days, exclude both event days; any other count excludes the first event's day and includes the second's.
    WHEN WA THEN
        IF `clear days, or at least a number of days`
        THEN JUST ((Day secondEvent MINUS Day firstEvent) MINUS 1)
        ELSE JUST (Day secondEvent MINUS Day firstEvent)
    -- SA: no such rule in sa-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN SA THEN NOTHING
    -- Tas: no such rule in tas-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN Tas THEN NOTHING
    -- ACT: act-interpretation-time `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the number of days between 2 events` (both event days excluded).
    WHEN ACT THEN
        IF `clear days, or at least a number of days`
        THEN JUST ((secondEvent MINUS firstEvent) MINUS 1)
        ELSE NOTHING
    -- NT: no such rule in nt-interpretation-time (answers NOTHING).
    WHEN NT THEN NOTHING
